      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to first expand the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and then identify the coefficients \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\). Finally, we will calculate the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\).\n\nLet's start by expanding the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\):\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's compute each term:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the coefficients are:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n= -48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\n\\[\n= (-48 + 124) + (-86 + 28)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 76 - 58\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
