      "text": "To find the expression for \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\), we start by expanding the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\).\n\nFirst, we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials, but extended to polynomials):\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms. The terms involving \\(x^3\\) are \\(-6x^3\\), the terms involving \\(x^2\\) are \\(21x^2 + 10x^2 = 31x^2\\), the terms involving \\(x\\) are \\(-35x - 8x = -43x\\), and the constant terms are \\(28\\):\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we identify the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48, \\quad 4(31) = 124, \\quad 2(-43) = -86, \\quad 28 = 28\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
